  "scope": "Restore perspective rendering. Planar rooms (JSON planar flag) use a grid-aligned top-down view with the engine pole-safety offset of 0.005 radians. Spatial rooms use 45 degree pitch and 10 degree yaw. Both fit the active map to 85 percent coverage. Portal transitions interpolate radius, target and orientation with source first-frame continuity. Exterior object groups in spatial rooms use actual finite camera-to-board/player sightline intersection against animated world AABBs, applying a shared 15 percent opacity material only to occluders and restoring it when they move away. Current-room geometry, child previews and planar exteriors keep their base materials. Geometry dimensions are weakly cached; opacity variants reuse bounded material caches. Browser fixtures cover both modes, real material opacity/restoration, model identity, mixed-mode entry/exit, desktop/mobile, recursive and ordinary portals. Boxbound-only validation; no engine edits, full repository tests or live tab/save changes."
